## Back-End — Testing

When writing or changing tests in **tradeup-api**, follow **[docs/back-end/tests.md](../../../docs/back-end/tests.md)** and **[docs/back-end/architecture.md](../../../docs/back-end/architecture.md)** (layer boundaries).

**Do**

- Name cases **`should …`**; assert **behaviour**, not mock trivia ([testing anti-patterns](../../../docs/shared/testing-anti-patterns.md)).
- Test **domain** and **use cases** with **fakes** or in-memory repositories — no full Laravel boot for pure logic.
- Use **`RefreshDatabase`** (or project trait) for **infrastructure** and **feature** tests that need the schema.
- Prefer **HTTP feature tests** for delivery contracts; **unit tests** for orchestration inside use cases.

**Don’t**

- Put **business rules** only reachable through tests; production code must encode invariants.
- Hit **real external APIs** in CI — `Http::fake()` or port + fake.
- Use **heavy Mockery** everywhere when a **small fake class** keeps tests readable.

Commands: `php artisan test` from `tradeup-api`.

